MEASURED + IMPLEMENTED 2026-08-19 (wire lane, commit a0d43c6) -- BUT NOT AS DECIDED. THE DECISION'S PREMISE IS FALSE.

The maintainer's decision was 'refuse in assert_representable', resting on
'YAML -0.0 has no representation'. That was derived from a single spelling
(-0, the canonical text, which yaml.v3 resolves as an INTEGER) and never
measured against any other. Measured now, sops 3.13.3, one document per
spelling, unencrypted leaf, digest -0:

  0            sops -d exit 51   self-MAC FAIL   (what YAML::XS renders)
  -0           sops -d exit 51   self-MAC FAIL   (the canonical text)
  !!float -0   sops -d exit 51   self-MAC FAIL
  -0.0         sops -d exit 0    self-MAC OK     reads back as -0
  -0.          sops -d exit 0    self-MAC OK

A representation exists, so refusing would have croaked on a value that
works. Two further measurements make a refusal in assert_representable
actively wrong, both of which the ticket's plan did not consider:

  * an ENCRYPTED -0.0 works today in BOTH formats (sops -d exit 0, reads
    back -0). assert_representable runs over encrypted leaves too, so a
    refusal there breaks it -- exactly the ADR 0008 objection.
  * JSON -0.0 works today. assert_representable is format-blind, so a
    refusal there breaks it too -- the trap this ticket flagged.

Implemented the repair instead (option 'reparieren', which the ticket
preferred and rejected only on the false premise): -0 leaves
$NO_AGREED_FORM in Encrypted.pm and Format::YAML::_float_carrier writes
-0.0. Byte movement verified by emitting 31 floats/strings/ints through
both handlers before and after: EXACTLY ONE LINE MOVES (the YAML negative
zero). JSON counter-measurement green before and after.

ADR 0006 amended (karr #62 paragraph); no new ADR -- trigger and
consequence are ADR 0006's own, and the -0 exclusion lived there.
Tests: t/24-float-precision.t section 9, 3 subtests, all against the
binary. Counter-proof: fix reverted -> subtest 19 red, rest green.
prove -lr t/ 661/661 PASS. SOPS_BIN=/tmp/sops prove -l t/04-interop.t
31/31 PASS, EXECUTED.

Also measured and worth knowing: sops CANNOT write this value either.
sops -e on a plaintext -0.0 emits -0 and then rejects its own file with
exit 51, in YAML and in JSON alike. So there is no sops->us fixture.

MAINTAINER: if you still want the refusal, this is one commit (a0d43c6)
